== ``` emacs```
``` emacs``` is a text editing utility in the linux shell.

The following shortcuts are important.
- *^x + ^c* quits.
- *^x + ^s* saves a file.
- *^x + ^f* opens a file.
- *^k* kills the process.
- *^y* yanks (pastes) previously killed text. 
- *^s* forward searchs.
- *^r* reverse searchs.
- *^\_* undos last change.
- *^x + ^b* lists all buffers.
- *^x + k* kills the current buffer.
- *^x + 1* shows the current buffer.
- *^x + 2* shows two buffers side by side.
- *^g* cancels the current command.
